From 2d13256dc24a9d0bba6b9f45431a1823803c57e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:24:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): revert #3053's contour lead seam change; main is red

PR #3053 (issue #3019) changed lead_fit for every closed contour, not only
rings with tabs: on a plain rectangle the seam moved from the corner to the
middle of an edge, the vertical entry arc reversed, and an oblique first cut
lost its chord-fan entry. motion's vertical_arc_entry caught it after the
merge (an_x_aligned_first_cut_enters_on_one_g18_arc_per_level,
an_oblique_first_cut_stays_chords_and_says_so_once); the PR's quick gate had
not run that suite. Reverting restores main; #3019 is reopened to be redone
so the change applies only where tabs need it.

Fixes #3111
Refs #3019

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
